# Scene system rule

SceneConfig is authoritative for projection-space scene content.

Preserve these invariants:

1. `scene.projectionId` is authoritative even if only one projection exists.
2. `scene.viewMode` is authoritative even if only full-world fixed view exists.
3. `scene.baseMap.id` is a durable base-map family id.
4. Scene layers are ordered deterministically.
5. Equal layer orders preserve array order.
6. Base map stays below overlays.
7. Projection defines spatial truth.
8. Base maps never define spatial truth.
9. Scene view and projection are separate concepts. Camera is a view transform, not a projection change and not a mutation of entity/time state ([ADR 0026](docs/decisions/0026-scene-camera-independent-of-projection-and-reference-frame.md)).
10. Chrome is not a scene layer and is not transformed by the scene camera.
11. Scene/map reference frame (Earth-fixed default; Moon/Sun/ISS/city/planet longitude-lock and position-lock; [LIB-083](docs/work/LIB-083-moon-longitude-locked-scene-frame.md)–[LIB-092](docs/work/LIB-092-city-and-planet-tracking-targets.md), [ADR 0027](docs/decisions/0027-moon-longitude-lock-is-a-scene-reference-frame.md)–[ADR 0036](docs/decisions/0036-city-and-planet-tracking-reuses-structured-target-identity.md)) is independent of camera. User-facing tracking is Tracking target + Tracking mode mapping into Earth-fixed or one anchored production type. `TrackableMapObjectId` is `"moon" | "sun" | "iss"` or structured `{ kind: "city", id }` / `{ kind: "planet", id }`. Target resolution is separate from frame math. ISS/city/planet tracking requires a valid authoritative position from the same payload used to paint. Do not implement entity-fixed by overwriting camera centre. Position-lock automatic scene-cover zoom is camera policy (`lockMode: "position"`), not a frame change and not target-specific. Clicking a rendered Moon, Sun, ISS, city-pin, or current-planet glyph sets Tracking target through `setTrackingTarget`; remembered mode is retained. Milky Way and earthquakes are not click-to-track.

Do not collapse source, presentation, lifecycle, and rendering behavior into one structure.

For new scene features, update or add tests at the resolver, composition, layer state, or RenderPlan builder boundary.
